license: EUPL-1.2
keywords:
  - twin transition
  - agent-based model
  - inequality
  - policy simulation
  - READJUST
  - Horizon Europe
abstract: >-
  Hybrid agent-based simulation of the EU green and digital (twin) transition,
  exposing how regional administrative absorption capacity shapes the
  distributional outcomes of transition policy. 97-parameter calibrated
  manifest; six NUTS-anchored regional archetypes; seeded, reproducible runs.
  Developed within the READJUST project, EU Horizon Europe GA 101132562.
